b/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717515}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4de9405f-1520-54e1-92d3-e7ba15edacd2" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nEnter the entries of $ABC$ in the table.\n\n| |Column 1|Column 2|Column 3|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|Row 1|{{field-1}}|{{field-2}}|{{field-3}}|\n|Row 2|{{field-4}}|{{field-5}}|{{field-6}}|\n|Row 3|{{field-7}}|{{field-8}}|{{field-9}}|\n" :question/worked-solution "The associative law lets us change the parentheses while keeping the factors in order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC &= (AB)C \\\\ &= A(BC).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll three matrices are $3\\times3$, so the intermediate dimensions alone do not favor either grouping. Computing $BC$ reveals cancellations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &= \\begin{bmatrix}1+1+1 & -2+1+1 & -2+4-2 \\\\ 1-1 & -2-1 & -2+2 \\\\ 1-1 & 1-1 & 4+2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &= \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying $A$ on the right by this diagonal matrix scales its first, second, and third columns by $3$, $-3$, and $6$, respectively. The order matters; scaling the rows would compute $(BC)A$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC &= A(BC) \\\\ &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &= \\begin{bmatrix}2(3) & (-1)(-3) & 3(6) \\\\ 1(3) & 4(-3) & (-2)(6) \\\\ (-3)(3) & 2(-3) & 1(6)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &= \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 & 18 \\\\ 3 & -12 & -12 \\\\ -9 & -6 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717512 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ef29583-be73-5980-8d53-68f660e2e88a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717488} {:answer/id #uuid "150f1212-c36c-5327-9ff4-701d25e51245" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717489} {:answer/id #uuid "718d92d6-5312-536e-b358-cd9a1482dc89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717501} {:answer/id #uuid "7e631623-92b3-55b0-89fe-0f0b25a42b39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717503} {:answer/id #uuid "eba655fb-9dd8-5371-9639-7d8bd9eb4c13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "150f1212-c36c-5327-9ff4-701d25e51245" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717489} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd04e184-95a0-5c52-8977-6d147ff8c13c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717518}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bcf22643-b2bf-5f10-8849-53af9f98e84a" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\quad B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "The associative law lets us change the parentheses while keeping the factors in order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC &= (AB)C \\\\ &= A(BC).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe dimensions are $2\\times3$, $3\\times1$, and $1\\times2$. Thus $AB$ has two entries, while $BC$ has six. Compute $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &= \\begin{bmatrix}1\\cdot2+2\\cdot(-1)+(-1)\\cdot1 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot2+1\\cdot(-1)+3\\cdot1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &= \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow form the outer product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC &= (AB)C \\\\ &= \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &= \\begin{bmatrix}(-1)(-1) & (-1)\\cdot2 \\\\ (-2)(-1) & (-2)\\cdot2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717517 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d09174e-09bf-5b77-834b-0ea2907def05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d09174e-09bf-5b77-834b-0ea2907def05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717491} :answer-field/id #uuid "34a48b03-ed51-5446-a1ef-25d59a473f4e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717494} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b822726-da80-5d23-8e6b-1b5a957534d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b822726-da80-5d23-8e6b-1b5a957534d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717507} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4714672-a915-54be-9dbf-96a255f0d855" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717514} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c58f13a-10e5-5107-b4d4-ed1db55cb014" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c58f13a-10e5-5107-b4d4-ed1db55cb014" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717496} :answer-field/id #uuid "d646d175-1236-5216-92e2-0712696f7619" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717516}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d9d4351a-47f8-548b-9f66-bfc9fe039836" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3\\end{bmatrix},\\quad B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\quad C=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nEnter the entries of $ABC$ in the table.\n\n| |Column 1|Column 2|Column 3|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|Row 1|{{field-1}}|{{field-2}}|{{field-3}}|\n" :question/worked-solution "The associative law lets us change the parentheses while keeping the factors in order:\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nHere $AB$ is $1\\times1$, whereas $BC$ is $2\\times3$. Computing $AB$ first gives one entry instead of six. We obtain\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\cdot1+(-3)\\cdot2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -4 & -12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717846 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9587160-501f-5278-bc32-0d3d22e9e96b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9587160-501f-5278-bc32-0d3d22e9e96b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717869} :answer-field/id #uuid "80c44925-fe99-5d45-af55-77281e7cf28f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717863} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "717fbadb-fb4b-5987-b409-093097542689" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "717fbadb-fb4b-5987-b409-093097542689" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717861} :answer-field/id #uuid "caada6e8-4330-5e94-8386-391f11b5ca66" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717870}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0ac18170-ef25-5b5a-a770-d4367fbe3f73" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nEnter the entries of the product.\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$ABC=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "The associative law changes the grouping while preserving factor order:\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nThe intermediate $AB$ is $2\\times2$; $BC$ is $2\\times1$. Compute $BC$ first. For example, the first entry is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(BC)_{1,1} &=(0)\\cdot(-3)+(0)\\cdot(-2) \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe complete product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Now complete the product. For example, the first entry is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(ABC)_{1,1} &=(0)\\cdot(0)+(2)\\cdot(5) \\\\ &=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe complete product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC &=A(BC) \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717847 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68a51a25-545f-5586-965d-9e48944af386" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68a51a25-545f-5586-965d-9e48944af386" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717860} :answer-field/id #uuid "03004ba9-81cd-5fc9-a562-fc3c806f258e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "111bedc5-9d1d-5bd9-ad06-6bd397d88e10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "111bedc5-9d1d-5bd9-ad06-6bd397d88e10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717848} :answer-field/id #uuid "1254b80d-76d6-51be-a247-4c0f36ce3c01" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717849} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a963a9a2-0c94-50b2-a83b-ac22da2e59b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a963a9a2-0c94-50b2-a83b-ac22da2e59b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717867} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fd825d4-94d2-5d6a-a676-5c309837e205" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717852}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0eb3c664-ebfe-5233-b012-18af315068d0" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nEnter the entries of the product.\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$ABC=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "The associative law changes the grouping while preserving factor order:\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nThe intermediate $AB$ is $3\\times2$; $BC$ is $1\\times1$. Compute $BC$ first. For example, the first entry is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(BC)_{1,1} &=(0)\\cdot(3)+(1)\\cdot(3) \\\\ &=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe complete product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Now complete the product. For example, the first entry is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(ABC)_{1,1} &=(-3)\\cdot(3) \\\\ &=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe complete product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC &=A(BC) \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717854 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5e238f1-b0e3-5190-ae0b-5c3168719610" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5e238f1-b0e3-5190-ae0b-5c3168719610" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717866} :answer-field/id #uuid "920d2606-98ae-5225-8c4c-454dfbfc011f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717864} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbc9bac0-426d-5ada-bb20-1dcc2d562015" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbc9bac0-426d-5ada-bb20-1dcc2d562015" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717874} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ea5d8a8-6d1b-5c62-91aa-1a92f8b85e1b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717865} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19f34538-3635-5fa6-b029-8e823c85a380" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19f34538-3635-5fa6-b029-8e823c85a380" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717851} :answer-field/id #uuid "d12e96a3-a04e-5fbf-88c1-380f9be21b52" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717871}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "378b0aa7-a5aa-5421-83cc-86d55546e160" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nEnter the entries of the product.\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$ABC=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "The associative law changes the grouping while preserving factor order:\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nThe intermediate $AB$ is $1\\times1$; $BC$ is $2\\times3$. Compute $AB$ first. For example, the first entry is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(AB)_{1,1} &=(-2)\\cdot(1)+(0)\\cdot(1) \\\\ &=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe complete product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB &=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Now complete the product. For example, the first entry is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(ABC)_{1,1} &=(-2)\\cdot(-3) \\\\ &=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe complete product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC &=(AB)C \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717857 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8b6699b-f789-55c5-9913-55cc4e29487f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8b6699b-f789-55c5-9913-55cc4e29487f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717873} :answer-field/id #uuid "40f5c402-bb92-5980-9d96-f71ff09f6c37" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717855} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47404218-5f28-5f21-8bfa-98aba6230260" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47404218-5f28-5f21-8bfa-98aba6230260" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717856} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e42e205-da31-587b-b6ba-afc92ce5e0e2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717862}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5acfa434-e50c-5670-b4df-8bce2efad04b" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nEnter the entries of the product.\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$ABC=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "The associative law changes the grouping while preserving factor order:\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nThe intermediate $AB$ is $1\\times2$; $BC$ is $2\\times2$. Compute $AB$ first. For example, the first entry is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(AB)_{1,1} &=(-2)\\cdot(2)+(3)\\cdot(-1) \\\\ &=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe complete product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB &=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -13\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Now complete the product. For example, the first entry is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(ABC)_{1,1} &=(-7)\\cdot(3)+(-13)\\cdot(0) \\\\ &=-21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe complete product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC &=(AB)C \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -13\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-21 & -34\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717875 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b926cb40-1318-5b69-89b8-d2bc6b5f920f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b926cb40-1318-5b69-89b8-d2bc6b5f920f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717868} :answer-field/id #uuid "16a2fa81-3505-597c-b5ac-ffe42866e3df" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717850} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid